|> Exercise
    handle=_complete_square_2_

    Solve Exercise >>_complete_square_1_ using
    algebra _&_ variables.

    |> Solution

        Put unknowns “$U$” and “$V$” for the two sets of dots. Then
        $$
        (x + U)^2 + V = x^2 + 10x + 30
        $$
        becomes the equation to satisfy.
        Expanding the left-hand side, we get:
        $$
        x^2 + 2Ux + U^2 + V = x^2 + 10x + 30.
        $$
        For this equation to hold for all $x$, corresponding
        coefficients must match on both sides:
        $$
        1 = 1
        $$
        (equating the coefficients of $x^2$), and
        $$
        2U = 10
        $$
        (equating the coefficients of $x$), and
        $$
        U^2 + V = 30
        $$
        (equating the constant terms). Only the
        latter two equations contain information.
        In particular,
        $$
        2U = 10
        $$
        implies $U = 5$, so $U^2 + V = 30$ becomes
        $25 + V = 30$, and
        $V = 30 - 25 = 5$.
        So $U = V = 5$, as previously found.
        (But now we know that the solution is _unique_,
        because $2U = 10$ forces $U = 5$,
        and $25 + V = 30$ forces $V = 5$.)
